.TH RED-AI 1 "March 2026" "red-ai 2.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
red-ai \- AI-powered RHEL system configuration tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B red-ai
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIPROMPT\fR ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B red-ai
is an AI-powered command-line tool for Red Hat Enterprise Linux (RHEL) system
administration. Users describe configuration tasks in plain English, and
.B red-ai
generates the appropriate Linux commands, previews them for approval, and
optionally executes them.
.PP
The tool uses a local database of 230+ RHEL command patterns for instant
offline responses. When available, it falls back to an Ollama-hosted LLM
(Mistral-based) for queries not covered by the local database.
.PP
All generated commands are displayed with risk levels (low, medium, high)
and require explicit confirmation before execution. Every execution is
logged for auditing purposes.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B PROMPT
A natural language description of the desired system configuration task.
Multiple words are joined automatically (no quoting required).
.sp
Examples:
.RS
.nf
red-ai disable SELinux
red-ai set vm.swappiness to 10
red-ai enable kdump
red-ai configure NTP with chrony
.fi
.RE
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-dry\-run
Preview the generated commands without executing them. Does not require root
privileges. Useful for reviewing what
.B red-ai
would do before running it for real.
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Skip all confirmation prompts and execute commands immediately. Use with
caution, especially for high-risk operations. Intended for scripting and
automation workflows where interactive confirmation is not possible.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version number and exit.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-info
Display detected system information including RHEL version, kernel version,
SELinux status, firewalld status, and other relevant system details. Useful
for verifying what
.B red-ai
knows about the current system.
.TP
.BR \-\-history " [\fIN\fR]"
Show the last
.I N
command executions from the audit log (default: 10). Each entry includes the
original prompt, generated commands, execution results, timestamps, and risk
levels.
.SH FEATURES
.SS Local Command Database
The built-in database covers 230+ common RHEL administration tasks organized
by category: networking, storage, security, kernel tuning, services, users,
packages, firewall, SELinux, NFS, NTP, DNS, kdump, and more.
.SS Ollama AI Fallback
When the local database cannot match a request, red-ai queries a locally
running Ollama instance with a custom Mistral-based model trained on RHEL
administration patterns. The Ollama service must be running on localhost:11434.
.SS kdump Preflight Checks
When enabling kdump, red-ai automatically performs preflight checks:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
Verifies crashkernel boot parameter is set
.IP \(bu 2
Checks that kexec-tools package is installed
.IP \(bu 2
Inspects kdump service status (active and enabled)
.RE
.PP
Missing prerequisites are added to the command list automatically.
.SS Sysctl Persistence
For sysctl parameter changes, red-ai prompts for the persistence mode:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
\fBRuntime + Persistent\fR \- applies immediately and survives reboot
.IP \(bu 2
\fBRuntime only\fR \- applies immediately but lost after reboot
.IP \(bu 2
\fBPersistent only\fR \- written to /etc/sysctl.d/ and applied on next reboot
.RE
.SS Risk Levels
Every command is tagged with a risk level:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
\fBlow\fR \- read-only or informational commands (e.g., status checks)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBmedium\fR \- configuration changes that can be reversed (e.g., sysctl)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBhigh\fR \- potentially destructive or hard-to-reverse operations (e.g., disk formatting, SELinux mode changes)
.RE
.SS Execution Logging
All command executions are logged to \fB/var/log/red-ai/\fR with automatic
log rotation. Logs include timestamps, prompts, commands, exit codes, and
output for audit compliance.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Preview commands to disable transparent hugepages:
.B red-ai --dry-run disable transparent hugepages
.TP
Enable IP forwarding with automatic confirmation:
.B red-ai -y enable ip forwarding
.TP
Check system information:
.B red-ai --info
.TP
View last 5 executions:
.B red-ai --history 5
.TP
Configure kdump with preflight checks:
.B red-ai enable kdump
.TP
Tune kernel parameters:
.B red-ai set vm.swappiness to 10
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful completion.
.TP
.B 1
An error occurred: no prompt given, command generation failed, user aborted,
or root privileges required but not available.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/log/red-ai/
Execution audit logs with automatic rotation.
.TP
.I /etc/sysctl.d/
Persistent sysctl configuration files created by red-ai.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OLLAMA_HOST
Override the Ollama API endpoint (default: http://localhost:11434).
.SH REQUIREMENTS
.IP \(bu 2
Python 3.6 or later (stdlib only, no external dependencies)
.IP \(bu 2
Root privileges for execution mode (dry-run works without root)
.IP \(bu 2
RHEL 7, 8, or 9
.IP \(bu 2
Ollama (optional, for AI-enhanced responses)
